"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; all funds governmental (School Nutrition is in Other Governmental Funds, so no business-type funds). Receipts/disbursements/balances use the Total Governmental Funds column (p3-4); the p4 total column prints transfers blank (General out 136,100 = School Nutrition 90,000 + Activities 46,100 in; nets to zero). Balance sheet uses the p2 net position section (modified cash basis; no liabilities). Statement General Fund column combines General, Depreciation and Employee Benefit funds (beginning 3,150,029 = 2,826,298 + 305,573 + 18,158). Transfer cross-check: General transfers out 136,100 (p9 line 8000) matches nutrition 90,000 (p12) + activities 46,100 (p15); the Depreciation Fund transfer to General 32,387 (p10) matches General transfer in 32,387 (p7) and is spent as Safety Grant 32,387 (p9); it is internal to the combined General column and eliminated in the statement, so no hidden transfer remains in the total column (statement General disbursements 4,930,994 = schedule 5,067,094 - 136,100). General Fund schedule lines with only a budget and no actual (e.g. 1420/23, 4512, 4527, 4708, and function headings with budget only) were skipped. Activities Fund has no printed totals so no detail_totals. Detail is function-level only (no object breakdown printed), so detail_category is not itemized. Fund schedule shows Special Building 133 as PPD sales tax but statement p3 shows it as Carline tax. Read pages 1-10 and 11-15 of 15."
